\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s1\fi-907\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\kerning28\b\caps 1.0\tab\page PURPOSE\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\qj\kerning0\b0\caps0 This procedure specifies the schedule and requirements for maintenance, performance and calibration of laboratory testing equipment. Meeting the criteria in this procedure demonstrates control of the maintenance and calibration parameters needed to achieve the accuracy of instruments used for testing purpose.\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s1\fi-907\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\kerning28\b\caps 2.0\tab SCOPE\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\qj\kerning0\b0\caps0 The procedure applies to all sections of lab. \par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s1\fi-907\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\kerning28\b\caps 3.0\tab RESPONSIBILITY\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\kerning0\caps0 3.1.\tab Lab Management System Coordinator (LMSC) \par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\qj\b0 LMSC has to ensure that the laboratory is equipped with the needed instruments and equipment that, at a minimum, meets the specifications of the analytical and testing methods employed.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-720\li720\sb120\sa120\sl26\slmult0\qj\b 3.1.1.\tab\b0 To ensure that equipment maintenance and calibration are conducted.\par
\b 3.1.2.\tab\b0 For providing support for arranging non-routine instrument repair and ordering of replacement instrument part.\par
\b 3.1.3.\tab\b0 Designating Technician where needed to perform periodic equipment checks.\par
\b 3.1.4.\tab\b0 To inspect the equipment received back after calibration and repair in consultation with Deputy Analyst. \par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s1\fi-907\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\kerning28\b\caps 4.0\tab PROCEDURE\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-720\li720\sb120\sa120\sl26\slmult0\qj\kerning0\caps0 4.1.1.\tab\b0 All relevant and useable equipment in the ESPAK lab are labeled with a unique identification number.\par
\b 4.1.2.\tab\b0 Following Equipment Identification Tag is displayed on every equipment\par

