\pard\widctlpar\sb120\qj Format for equipment code is LAB-EQP-NNN, \par
Where\tab\par
\b ESP\b0\tab\tab Environment Service Protection\par
\b LAB\b0\tab\tab  Laboratory\par
\b EQP\b0\tab\tab  stands for equipment\par
\b NNN\tab\b0\tab  represents equipment number starting from 01, 02, 03 and so on.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-720\li720\sb120\sa120\sl26\slmult0\qj\b 4.1.3.\tab\b0 Master List of Equipment is maintained in the Laboratory by LMS Coordinator in which equipment details are entered with code and serial for effective traceability.\par
\b 4.1.4.\tab\b0 For new instruments the laboratory may determine independently that quality assurance specifications have been met. Equipment is not used until this has been completed and users have been trained in its operation.\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\b 4.2.\tab Equipment Maintenance and Performance Checks\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-720\li720\sb120\sa120\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.2.1.\tab\b0 Manufacturer\rquote s instructions are used for guidance in performing equipment maintenance. In the absence of manufacturer\rquote s instructions, instructions are provided in the form or a work instruction where required.\par
\b 4.2.2.\tab\b0 Use of outside contractors to perform repairs or maintenance depends on the type of repair/ maintenance.\par
\b 4.2.3.\tab\b0 Such maintenance and performance checks are documented in Equipment Maintenance Log Book.\par
\b 4.2.4.\tab\b0 The Equipment Maintenance Log Books are compiled and required information is maintained in a readily accessible manner. These log books are placed in a secure and accessible place in the laboratory.\par
\b 4.2.5.\tab\b0 The records for all main equipment are kept in respective log books. \par
\b 4.2.6.\tab\b0 Preventive maintenance of equipment is performed by qualified laboratory staff, which includes cleaning of equipment after completing the testing activities and conducting general service as per the instructions in respective operation manuals provided by the manufacturer if available.\par
\b 4.2.7.\tab\b0 Instrument and equipment repairs are documented, the documentation includes,\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-360\li1440\sb120\sa120\sl26\slmult0\qj\f5\'d8\tab\f1 Initials of the Deputy Analysts and the date the problem was observed.\par
\f5\'d8\tab\f1 Description of the problem / fault\par
\f5\'d8\tab\f1 Date and initials of the Deputy Analysts or service representative performing the repair.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-720\li720\sb120\sa120\sl26\slmult0\qj\b 4.2.8.\tab\b0  If limits or specifications are exceeded, explanatory documentation is required. Documentation includes the limit of specifications that was exceeded and the probable cause and resolution, such documentation is also recorded in Equipment Maintenance Log Books.\par
\b 4.2.9.\tab\b0 Corrective and Preventive Action Form is raised when corrective and / or preventive actions are required for equipment and / or peripherals.\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\b 4.3.\tab Equipment Calibration\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\qj\b0 All calibration especially in the scope of accreditation is conducted by external calibration laboratory preferably an accredited lab. Calibration data is updated on the Master List of Equipment form.\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\b 4.4.\tab Unserviceable Equipment\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-720\li720\sb120\sa120\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.4.1.\tab\b0 Equipment is considered \ldblquote UNSERVICEABLE\rdblquote  as its status, in case of any of the following situation:\par

\pard\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\qj\f5\'d8\tab\f1 Damaged\par
\f5\'d8\tab\f1 Does not give correct readings\par
\f5\'d8\tab\f1 Unfit for use due to any reason\par
\f5\'d8\tab\f1 Obsolete\par
\f5\'d8\tab\f1 Awaiting calibration / repair\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-720\li720\sa120\sl26\slmult0\qj\b 4.4.2.\tab\b0 Such equipment is tagged as \ldblquote Unserviceable\rdblquote  or \ldblquote U/S\rdblquote . An entry must be made in Monthly Unserviceable State Form for all unserviceable equipment.\par
\b 4.4.3.\tab\b0 Out of service equipment must be calibrated or verified prior to use.\par
\b 4.4.4.\tab\b0 Equipment that is not operating properly is clearly marked to show that it is out of service.\par
\b 4.4.5.\tab\b0 When an instrument is discovered to be improperly operating, it is tagged and taken out of service.\par
\b 4.4.6.\tab\b0 Equipment is not returned to service until performance checks and calibration have been performed and documented in Equipment Maintenance Log Books. \par
\b 4.4.7.\tab\b0 An exception may be made if the equipment failure is not directly related to its analytical function, such as a problem with peripheral equipment. For example, if monitor attached to a spectrophotometer is out of order, performance checks and verification for the spectrophotometer may not be needed repair.\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\b 4.5.\tab Handling, Use, Transportation and Storage of Equipment\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-720\li720\sb120\sa120\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.5.1.\tab Handling and Use of Equipment\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\qj\b0 The work instruction defines the handling and use of the equipment. Equipment is operated by authorized personnel; authorized personnel are \tab identified in Lab Authorization Permits. In case maintenance / operation \tab manuals are provided by the equipment manufacturer. They are either attached with the Equipment Maintenance Log Book or its reference is mentioned in the said log book\cf2 .\cf0  The location of equipment is also recorded in the same.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-720\li720\sb120\sa120\sl26\slmult0\qj\b 4.5.2.\tab Transportation of Equipment\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\qj\b0 Equipment is transported through company / vendor vehicles with proper packing and if there are special requirements w.r.t the transportation of the equipment they are accounted and if deemed necessary by lab staff the requirements are communicated to concerned personnel.\par
After calibration / service is performed, equipment is received and inspection is carried out by Deputy Analyst in coordination with LMS Coordinator who verifies that equipment is meeting the requirement of testing.\par
When the equipment is cleared after inspection it is put into service otherwise it is labeled unserviceable and matter is brought into the notice of MR who decides further course of action.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-720\li720\sb120\sa120\sl26\slmult0\qj\b 4.5.3.\tab Storage of Equipment\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\qj\b0 Equipment in lab is stored at appropriate locations and areas where equipment is being kept for operations are labeled with their names, equipment code and their location number.\par
Test equipment is only allowed to be moved from its designated location in cases such as repair, maintenance or calibration requirements with approval of LMS Coordinator.\par

